  "response": "## The finding\n\n`crimes scan --format json` surfaces it as **`crime_00007` — Missing Agent Context** (`missing_agent_context`, medium severity, confidence 0.90). It's a repo-level finding, so ignore the `file: \"assets/cjs_shims.js\"` anchor — that's just where the detector pinned it, not where the problem lives.\n\nThe evidence is four negatives and one positive:\n\n```\nno AGENTS.md found at repo root\nno CLAUDE.md found at repo root\nno .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md present\nno .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md present\npackage.json declares bin(s): tsup, tsup-node — agents have no way to discover commands\n```\n\nSo: **no agent-facing surface at all.** Not a stale one, not a thin one — none of the four locations exist.\n\n## Why that matters *here* specifically\n\nA missing AGENTS.md is cheap in a small tidy repo. In this one it compounds with three other things the same scan reports, and that's the actual argument for fixing it before your first PR:\n\n**1. Every entry point is a God Function.** All 8 high-severity findings are `large_function`, and they sit exactly where a newcomer lands:\n\n| Symbol | File | Lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `build` | `src/index.ts` | 293 |\n| `runEsbuild` | `src/esbuild/index.ts` | 237 |\n| `mainTasks` | `src/index.ts` | 194 |\n| `main` | `src/cli-main.ts` | 153 |\n| `postcssPlugin` | `src/esbuild/postcss.ts` | 140 |\n| `getRollupConfig` | `src/rollup.ts` | 122 |\n\nAn agent with no orientation file opens `src/index.ts` (459 lines, fan-out 17), lands mid-`build`, and edits a 293-line body it has only partially loaded.\n\n**2. The hub files are unmarked.** `src/utils.ts` has fan-in 18 (p95 cutoff is 9), `src/plugin.ts` 10, `src/log.ts` 9. Nothing in the repo says \"these are load-bearing.\" Blast radius on `src/utils.ts` is 29 transitive importers.\n\n**3. The test suite will lie to you.** Twelve tests contain **zero** `expect`/`assert` calls (`test/example.test.ts`, `test/graphql.test.ts`, `test/shims.test.ts`, `test/tsconfig.test.ts`, `test/experimental-dts.test.ts` ×4, `test/index.test.ts`), and another ~14 use only weak matchers. An agent that changes `build`, runs the suite, sees green, and reports success has verified almost nothing. `src/index.ts`, `src/esbuild/index.ts`, and `src/utils.ts` all carry `test_gap: 0` in the scan — meaning tests *exist and touch them* — which makes the false confidence worse, not better.\n\nThe consequence chain: **no context file → agent doesn't know the commands, the hubs, or that the tests are hollow → confident edit to a 293-line function → green suite → wrong PR.** That's the failure mode `missing_agent_context` is scored for; its `agent_risk` (0.47) is the highest of any medium finding in the report.\n\n## Minimal AGENTS.md that clears the finding\n\nThe detector checks for presence at repo root, so any `AGENTS.md` clears it — but a stub that clears the finding without carrying the three facts above just moves the risk. This is the smallest version that actually earns it:\n\n```markdown\n# AGENTS.md\n\nBuild tool: `tsup`. Bundles TS/JS via esbuild, emits declarations via\nrollup/api-extractor. Published bins: `tsup`, `tsup-node`.\n\n## Commands\n\n<!-- FILL FROM package.json scripts — the scan only sees `bin`, not `scripts` -->\n- Install:   `pnpm install`\n- Build:     `pnpm build`\n- Test:      `pnpm test`\n- Typecheck: `pnpm typecheck`\n\nRun the full test suite before opening a PR. See the caveat below.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/index.ts`        — public API + `build()` orchestrator. Entry point for most work.\n- `src/cli-main.ts`     — CLI arg parsing and `main()`.\n- `src/esbuild/`        — esbuild pipeline and plugins (postcss, svelte, swc).\n- `src/rollup.ts`, `src/api-extractor.ts`, `src/tsc.ts` — declaration-file paths.\n- `src/plugins/`        — built-in output plugins.\n- `test/`               — integration tests; each spins a real build in a temp dir.\n\n## Load-bearing files — read importers before changing\n\n- `src/utils.ts`  (18 direct importers, 29 transitive)\n- `src/plugin.ts` (10 importers)\n- `src/log.ts`    (9 importers)\n\nPrefer additive changes here. Restructuring ripples across most of `src/`.\n\n## Large orchestrators\n\n`build` (src/index.ts), `runEsbuild` (src/esbuild/index.ts), and `main`\n(src/cli-main.ts) are each 150–300 lines. Read the whole function before\nediting any part of it — sections interact.\n\n## Testing caveat\n\nParts of the suite are assertion-free or use weak matchers, so a green run\ndoes not prove behaviour is preserved. If you change build output, add an\nassertion on the actual emitted files rather than relying on the existing test.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- TypeScript, ESM source, dual CJS/ESM output.\n- Options flow as a single `options` bag through most of the pipeline;\n  check `normalizeOptions` (src/index.ts) for defaulting before assuming a\n  field is set.\n```\n\nTwo things to flag: the **Commands** block is the one section I can't fill from the scan — `crimes` reports `bin` entries, not `scripts`, so read `package.json` and replace those four lines with the real ones. And the file belongs at the repo root as `AGENTS.md`; `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` would satisfy the detector equally, but `AGENTS.md` is the vendor-neutral choice for a repo with outside contributors.\n\nEffort is `small` and risk is `low` — it's a new file, nothing to break. Worth doing as its own commit before the PR rather than folded into it.",
